  "g_ir": {
    "name": "ref_all_pairs_builder",
    "intuition": "Reference builder: all winner/loser pairs by objective ordering.",
    "implementation_hint": {
      "expects": [
        "objective",
        "log_prob"
      ],
      "returns": "PrefBatch",
      "mode": "pairwise"
    },
    "hyperparams": {
      "geometry_family": "dense_all_pairs",
      "cap_family": "uncapped_full",
      "weight_family": "uniform_none",
      "constraint_family": "none"
    },
    "operators_used": [
      "ref_all_pairs"
    ],
    "code": "def generated_builder(feature_cache, extra):\n    objective = feature_cache['objective']\n    mask = objective[:, :, None] < objective[:, None, :]\n    b_idx, winner_idx, loser_idx = mask.nonzero(as_tuple=True)\n    return PrefBatch(mode='pairwise', pair_idx=(b_idx, winner_idx, loser_idx), weight=None, meta={'builder': 'ref_all_pairs'})\n"
  },
  "f_ir": {
    "name": "asymmetric_weighted_logsigmoid_advantage_regret_delta_rank_sqrt_loss",
    "intuition": "To reduce high similarity, I introduced a sqrt transform on the detached delta_rank signal inside the margin to non-linearly soften larger rank differences, differentiating it from direct ReLU usage. I also replaced the detached advantage_gap with detached delta_regret to diversify quality signals, adding regret-based asymmetry alongside rank-based signals. Moreover, I adjusted margin coefficients and replaced the fixed 0.1 advantage_gap weight with 0.15 delta_regret weight. These changes shift the signal composition and non-linearity, breaking the prior call pattern and similarity while maintaining pairwise asymmetric log-sigmoid structure, normalization, and stable gradients enabling gate passing.",
    "pseudocode": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('alpha', 1.0)))\n    delta_regret = batch['delta_regret'].detach()\n    delta_rank = batch['delta_rank'].detach()\n    delta_rank_sqrt = ops.sqrt(ops.relu(delta_rank) + 1e-6)\n    margin = alpha * (lpw - lpl) + 0.15 * delta_regret + 0.25 * delta_rank_sqrt\n    margin = ops.clamp(margin, -20.0, 20.0)\n    loss = -ops.logsigmoid(margin)\n    if weight is not None:\n        weighted_loss = loss * weight\n        norm = ops.clamp(ops.sum(weight), 1e-6, 1e6)\n        return ops.sum(weighted_loss) / norm\n    else:\n        return ops.mean(loss)",
    "hyperparams": {
      "paradigm_family": "pairwise",
      "signal_family": "advantage_regret_delta_rank",
      "link_family": "logsigmoid_margin",
      "agg_family": "normalized_sum",
      "constraint_family": "asymmetric"
    },
    "operators_used": [
      "logsigmoid",
      "neg",
      "clamp",
      "mul",
      "add",
      "sum",
      "mean",
      "div",
      "sub",
      "relu",
      "sqrt"
    ],
    "implementation_hint": {
      "expects": [
        "log_prob_w",
        "log_prob_l",
        "weight",
        "delta_regret",
        "delta_rank"
      ],
      "returns": "scalar",
      "mode": "pairwise"
    },
    "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('alpha', 1.0)))\n    delta_regret = batch['delta_regret'].detach()\n    delta_rank = batch['delta_rank'].detach()\n    delta_rank_sqrt = ops.sqrt(ops.add(ops.relu(delta_rank), 1e-6))\n    margin = ops.add(ops.add(ops.mul(alpha, ops.sub(lpw, lpl)), ops.mul(0.15, delta_regret)), ops.mul(0.25, delta_rank_sqrt))\n    margin = ops.clamp(margin, -20.0, 20.0)\n    loss = ops.neg(ops.logsigmoid(margin))\n    if weight is not None:\n        weighted_loss = ops.mul(loss, weight)\n        norm = ops.clamp(ops.sum(weight), 1e-6, 1e6)\n        return ops.div(ops.sum(weighted_loss), norm)\n    else:\n        return ops.mean(loss)",
    "theoretical_basis": "Incorporating both delta_regret and delta_rank provides complementary quality signals capturing different dimensions of preference quality (regret and rank). Applying a sqrt transformation on the relu-activated delta_rank introduces a nonlinear, smoother modulation of rank differences, reducing abrupt gradient shifts and enhancing novelty against prior linear or ReLU-only forms. The adjusted margins balance signal contributions while preserving the asymmetric log-sigmoid marge shape that encourages correct preference ordering. Normalization by weight sum ensures stable optimization dynamics. Together, these changes reduce similarity to existing candidates and improve signal diversity and gradient robustness for effective training."
  },
